*Cyte-09 expends {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''50''' energy to instantly [[Reload|reload]] his currently equipped weapon while throwing forward <u>'''2'''</u> ammo packs. Looting the [[Ammo]] packs will instantly refill the equipped weapon's magazine, triggering an [[Extra Hit]] of {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''10% / 15% / 20% / 25%''' damage ({{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''20% / 30% / 40% / 50%''' for [[Sniper Rifle]]s) that applies a forced status effect from the selected element. On cast, Cyte-09 automatically enhances his currently held primary weapon, secondary weapon, or {{A|Neutralize}}'s {{Weapon|Neutralizer}} sniper rifle with this bonus. Reloading the weapon (default {{Keybind|R}}) while buffed by Resupply will clear the elemental damage bonus. Ammo packs last <u>'''indefinitely'''</u> until collected and up to <u>'''6'''</u> ammo packs may be deployed on the field at once.
**All players in the squad have their own instances of Resupply's ammo packs, meaning that collecting an ammo pack for yourself will not take it away from a squad member.
*** For non-Cyte-09 allies, picking up an ammo pack uses a fixed value of '''10%''' damage for the Extra Hit ('''20%''' for Sniper Rifles), which is <u>'''not'''</u> affected by {{Stat|Ability Strength}}.
***For Cyte-09 and allies using him, picking up an ammo pack uses a fixed value of '''10% / 15% / 20% / 25%''' damage for the Extra Hit ('''20% / 30% / 40% / 50%''' for Sniper Rifles), which is <u>'''not'''</u> affected by {{Stat|Ability Strength}}.
**Resupply has a '''0.35''' second cooldown between casts.
**Resupply ammo packs use a unique model exclusive to Cyte-09, and display their elemental damage type icon overhead.
**All allied {{Faction|Tenno}} can see the elemental damage type icons on their mini-map to locate specific ammo packs.
**A fully loaded weapon can only gain one elemental damage bonus at a time. However, upon expending at least one ammo, a weapon that already has one of Resupply's elemental bonuses can gain an additional bonus by looting a Resupply ammo pack that was previously deployed.
**Resupply ammo packs only refill the current magazine, and will '''not''' restore any reserve ammo.
**[[Archgun]]s and [[:Category:Battery Weapons|battery weapons]] (including [[Kitgun]]s equipped with {{Arcane|Pax Charge}}) do '''not''' benefit from Resupply ammo packs.
* Casting Resupply is a [[One-Handed Action]]. As such, it can be used while performing various maneuvers and actions without interruption.
*Hold the ability to open a [[Gear]] wheel to select the elemental damage type of the reload and ammo packs: {{D|Heat}}, {{D|Cold}}, {{D|Electricity}}, {{D|Toxin}}, {{D|Blast}}, {{D|Radiation}}, {{D|Gas}}, {{D|Magnetic}}, {{D|Viral}}, {{D|Corrosive}}, randomized, or previously selected. Tap the ability to deploy the last selected element.
**Resupply's forced Status Effect will '''not''' apply if the enemy is killed in a single bullet, such as when using Neutralizer to headshot enemies. This prevents area of effect status like {{D|Gas}} or {{D|Blast}} from being effective for crowd control unless firing at enemies that are tough enough to survive a single shot.
**By default, tap cast starts as randomize.
**Elemental bonus does '''not''' override the {{D|Toxin}} damage bonus from {{WF|Oraxia}}'s {{A|Silken Stride}}.
**Elemental bonus can be overridden by the {{D|Heat}} damage bonus from {{WF|Uriel}}'s [[Uriel/Abilities/Passive|Demonium]], and vise versa.
***However, upon reloading to clear Resupply while Demonium is still active, Demonium's {{D|Heat}} bonus will be reapplied.
*'''Ability Synergy''': {{A|Neutralize}}'s {{Weapon|Neutralizer}} is a sniper rifle, and thus receives the doubled damage bonus from Resupply's elemental bonus.
